= Uniform Resource Identifier — Simple =

A Uniform Resource Identifier (URI) is a compact identifier for a resource defined according to a URI scheme.

URIs provide a general identification mechanism used throughout Web architecture and many non-Web systems. A URI can identify a resource without implying that the resource can be retrieved directly from a network location.

'''Important boundaries:'''
* URI ≠ network location necessarily
* URI ≠ domain name

